WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.405
Armenia had taken Christianity as its
faith early in the fourth century.

2
00:00:07.765 --> 00:00:12.735
In 449 Yazdegerd II,
shahanshah of Sasanian Persia,

3
00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:15.995
commanded the Armenians
to renounce Christianity

4
00:00:16.035 --> 00:00:17.984
for Zoroastrianism.

5
00:00:18.344 --> 00:00:21.282
In 450 much of Armenia rose.

6
00:00:21.322 --> 00:00:24.912
At the head of the rising
stood Vardan Mamikonian,

7
00:00:24.952 --> 00:00:28.961
sparapet, the hereditary commander
of Armenia's army.

8
00:00:29.321 --> 00:00:31.931
In 451 the Persian army came,

9
00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:35.577
with its elite cavalry
and a corps of war elephants.

10
00:00:35.617 --> 00:00:38.547
Vardan drew up his army
on the plain of Avarayr,

11
00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:40.567
by the river Tghmut.

12
00:00:40.927 --> 00:00:43.296
The Armenians won the first clashes.

13
00:00:43.336 --> 00:00:46.346
Then the Persian reserves
surrounded Vardan's men,

14
00:00:46.386 --> 00:00:48.186
and Vardan fell there.

15
00:00:48.764 --> 00:00:51.734
The field was lost,
yet the faith held:

16
00:00:51.774 --> 00:00:55.414
in 484 his nephew Vahan
won freedom of worship

17
00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.534
by the Treaty of Nvarsak.

18
00:00:57.894 --> 00:01:00.413
Stand where Vardan stood.

